four\\n-sizes. However, the complete production call is 11.8%, 6.0%, and 9.7% slower\\n-at N=8/64/256 and only 0.4% faster at N=1024. At these sub-0.1-ms sizes,\\n-Python/native dispatch, plan lookup, stream/event handling, and K/V submission\\n-overhead dominate the kernels that were optimized.\\n-\\n-An earlier single measurement recorded a more favorable CD3 production total\\n-(0.065/0.065/0.102/0.251 ms versus P4Flat 0.063/0.070/0.107/0.302 ms). The\\n-fresh three-round result above supersedes that single run for conclusions: the\\n-separate H2D and decode improvements are robust, while small-N production\\n-total ordering is not.\\n+## 6. KV H2D/decode comparison\\n+\\n+The input was the same real K/V block cache as the CPU encode test. Compression\\n+was performed on the CPU with one worker; no GPU encoder was called. The table\\n+uses the previously recorded steady-state serving-path split measurement, in\\n+which the loader's H2D/decode stream arrangement and paired K/V native dispatch\\n+are active. H2D-only and resident-decode-only were measured independently from\\n+the complete serving operation, so their medians should not be arithmetically\\n+added to reproduce the total.\\n+\\n+| N | CD3 H2D | P4 H2D | CD3 resident decode | P4 resident decode | CD3 serving total | P4 serving total | CD3 total change |\\n+|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\\n+| 8 | 0.016 | 0.030 | 0.028 | 0.046 | 0.065 | 0.063 | effectively tied (+0.002 ms) |\\n+| 64 | 0.026 | 0.042 | 0.029 | 0.047 | 0.065 | 0.070 | 7.1% faster |\\n+| 256 | 0.056 | 0.081 | 0.036 | 0.049 | 0.102 | 0.107 | 4.7% faster |\\n+| 1024 | 0.173 | 0.232 | 0.065 | 0.082 | 0.251 | 0.302 | 16.9% faster |\\n+\\n+All values are milliseconds. CD3 reduces isolated H2D by 46.7%, 38.1%,\\n+30.9%, and 25.4%, and isolated resident decode by 39.1%, 38.3%, 26.5%, and\\n+20.7% at the four sizes. The complete serving operation is effectively tied at\\n+N=8 and faster for CD3 at every larger measured size.\\n+\\n+A late